  "limits": "One Windows/native process observation, not a statistical or release gate. Ring latency excludes payload capture; thread allocation includes occurrence construction. Quiet driver claims after each call; full driver pauses consumption; contended driver uses four producers and one polling consumer of the real ring. Process CPU includes driver/consumer/CLR work. Logical producer RMW counts are derived from actual admissions/evictions and audited source sites (6 per admission plus 1 per eviction), not hardware instruction counters. Complete-caller rows include owned capture with the actual runtime consumer paused; the legacy-factory row separately records its simple callback\u0027s duration within total caller latency. These are not arbitrary application callback costs. Sampling buffers belong to the harness, not production storage."
